@format 1
@id section-modification.set-start-on-selected-section
@title Set Start on selected section
@section Section modification
@area In Split tab
@entry start-dispatch
@summary Modify the start boundary of the currently selected Split section; Set Start branches that create a new section are excluded.
@related section-modification.common.compass-buttons, section-modification.common.keyboard-shortcuts, section-modification.common.apply-modified-state, section-creation.set-start-creates-section
@tag section
@tag split
@tag modification
@tag start

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment
@alias piece = Cadroue.Core.LPiece

[start-dispatch] setStart dispatch request <input>
= The request came from the Split Compass Start button or the currently bound SectionStart shortcut.
> dispatch-guard

[dispatch-guard] Active Split flow guard <decision>
- PFlowShortcutDispatch requires a command-active flow with a loaded spool and active section UI before invoking PFlowStartSet @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / setStart
? "Rejected" > dispatch-rejected
? "Accepted" > handler-guard

[dispatch-rejected] Set Start ignored <output>
= No section operation is called.

[handler-guard] Modification preconditions <decision>
- PFlowStartSet requires section editing enabled, a loaded spool, and a nonblank source path before calling LSegmentStartSet with cursor, duration, color, and overlap policy @ flow.PFlowStartSet(...)
@ flow.PFlowColorRead(...)
@ property flow.PFlowOverlapAllowed
? "Editing disabled or media/source unavailable" > handler-rejected
? "Preconditions accepted" > branch-check

[handler-rejected] Set Start blocked <output>
= Existing section state is unchanged.

[branch-check] Existing-section branch <decision>
- LPieceStartSet creates instead when no section is selected or the selected section ends strictly before the cursor; only the remaining branch can modify the selected section @ segment.LSegmentStartSet(...)
@ piece.LPieceStartSet(...)
? "No selection or selected end before cursor" > creation-outside
? "Selected section reaches cursor" > end-bound-check

[creation-outside] Creation branch excluded <output>
= This path belongs to Section creation, not Section modification.

[end-bound-check] Cursor must stay before selected end <decision>
- The existing-section branch rejects a cursor at or after the selected section end @ piece.LPieceStartSet(...) / selected end check
? "Cursor at or after end" > invalid-start
? "Cursor before end" > floor-check

[invalid-start] No start modification <output>
= The selected section is unchanged and no modification log is written.

[floor-check] Respect previous-section floor <decision>
- When overlap is disabled, LPieceFloorRead finds the latest other section end at or before the selected section's original start; a cursor earlier than that floor is rejected. With overlap allowed the floor is zero @ piece.LPieceFloorRead(...)
@ piece.LPieceStartSet(...) / floor check
? "Cursor before allowed floor" > floor-rejected
? "Cursor allowed" > replace-start

[floor-rejected] Start extension blocked <output>
= The selected section is unchanged and no modification log is written.

[replace-start] Replace selected start boundary <process>
- Copy the section list and replace the selected LPiece with the same data except LPieceStart=cursor; even an unchanged start value still produces an apply plan @ piece.LPieceStartSet(...) / existing-section plan
> map:section-modification.common.apply-modified-state
